{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/975783-is-there-a-superhero-supervillan-game-similar-to-cofd","id":975783,"title":"Is there a superhero/supervillan game similar to CofD?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-24T19:47:43-07:00","id":975783,"title":"Is there a superhero/supervillan game similar to CofD?","content":"I want to play a superhero game, that runs very similar to something like CofD or VtR. A even better example would be the web serial Worm. The most important things are character customization, setting freedom, and toolbox style rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T20:06:27-07:00","id":975791,"title":"","content":"I think both Champions and Mutants &amp; Masterminds offers that.<br /> <br /> There's probably a lot more. Since superheroes are usually about the powers, the games tend to offer a lot in the way of character customization. And of course since superheroes can fit in a wide range of settings there's also that freedom, though they usually also offer a 'premade' setting or five.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T20:41:14-07:00","id":975803,"title":"","content":"Hm, you know, Onyx Path has the Trinity Games and Scion, both of which are similar in some ways to ChroD but much more superhero-y in focus. <br /> <br /> Mirrors has rules for &quot;dark heroes&quot;, but they're meant to be more of a mythological heroes deal. <br /> <br /> Also, with deepest apologies, Mage is pretty close to being a superhero game: you have a secret identity, you fight evil...and it does fit all the stuff that you're asking for. The magic creation rules are pretty flexible and easy, and ChroD is meant so you can change parts of it pretty easily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T21:25:03-07:00","id":975820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/975783-is-there-a-superhero-supervillan-game-similar-to-cofd?p=975803#post975803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm, you know, Onyx Path has the Trinity Games and Scion, both of which are similar in some ways to ChroD but much more superhero-y in focus.<br /> <br /> Mirrors has rules for &quot;dark heroes&quot;, but they're meant to be more of a mythological heroes deal.<br /> <br /> Also, with deepest apologies, Mage is pretty close to being a superhero game: you have a secret identity, you fight evil...and it does fit all the stuff that you're asking for. The magic creation rules are pretty flexible and easy, and ChroD is meant so you can change parts of it pretty easily.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wanted to stay away from myth and magic, more into the psionic powers, mutations, and super gadgets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T22:20:06-07:00","id":975835,"title":"","content":"Princess the Hopeful? It has literal Double Identity Protection, magical powers and items attached to your transformed state. And despite the name, you CAN play as a Prince instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T23:03:05-07:00","id":975842,"title":"","content":"I really enjoy Supers as a genre, and I have played a good number of supers systems.<br /> Probably the closest to what you are looking for is the original <b>Aberrant</b>. The baseline assumptions of the game are more like the deconstructionist style presented in &quot;Watchmen&quot;or &quot;the Authority&quot;. The game posits that the player characters are not &quot;super-heroes&quot; (although they can certainly try to be), but rather everyday people gifted with extraordinary power almost at random. Whether you use that power to save the world, make yourself a God, or burn it all down becomes a very personal question. Also, the mechanics are a version of the Storyteller system, so it is familiar to White Wolf veterans.<br /> <br /> Thematically, common elements included body horror, the corrupting nature of power, conspiracies,and transhumanism (among so many others).<br /> <br /> I do have a few criticisms; The mechanics do a decent enough job with the power system,but it far from perfect, and the setting material often focuses on pre-determined events and key NPC's to the point that a group of players can feel like bystanders in their own story (not an uncommon thing during that era of RPG's). But over all its a respectable game line.<br /> <br /> I ran an Aberrant game for several years and even contributed to few fan projects, so it has a special place in my heart and I am looking forward to the Storypath version.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T23:32:16-07:00","id":975852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/975783-is-there-a-superhero-supervillan-game-similar-to-cofd?p=975842#post975842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really enjoy Supers as a genre, and I have played a good number of supers systems.<br /> Probably the closest to what you are looking for is the original <b>Aberrant</b>. The baseline assumptions of the game are more like the deconstructionist style presented in &quot;Watchmen&quot;or &quot;the Authority&quot;. The game posits that the player characters are not &quot;super-heroes&quot; (although they can certainly try to be), but rather everyday people gifted with extraordinary power almost at random. Whether you use that power to save the world, make yourself a God, or burn it all down becomes a very personal question. Also, the mechanics are a version of the Storyteller system, so it is familiar to White Wolf veterans.<br /> <br /> Thematically, common elements included body horror, the corrupting nature of power, conspiracies,and transhumanism (among so many others).<br /> <br /> I do have a few criticisms; The mechanics do a decent enough job with the power system,but it far from perfect, and the setting material often focuses on pre-determined events and key NPC's to the point that a group of players can feel like bystanders in their own story (not an uncommon thing during that era of RPG's). But over all its a respectable game line.<br /> <br /> I ran an Aberrant game for several years and even contributed to few fan projects, so it has a special place in my heart and I am looking forward to the Storypath version.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad to hear about it, this may be what I'm looking for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T23:34:14-07:00","id":975853,"title":"","content":"I found something. It is a fan made project called Chronicles of Justice. It is designed based on CofD second edition, and looks really cool. <a href=\"http://chroniclesofjustice.com/rules.php\" target=\"_blank\">http://chroniclesofjustice.com/rules.php</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T01:07:57-07:00","id":975880,"title":"","content":"Onyx Path is currently working on a gameline called Deviant where you play as genetically altered beings/psionics/mutants/etc. on the run. So that might work when it comes out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T10:05:52-07:00","id":975991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/975783-is-there-a-superhero-supervillan-game-similar-to-cofd?p=975853#post975853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I found something. It is a fan made project called Chronicles of Justice. It is designed based on CofD second edition, and looks really cool. <a href=\"http://chroniclesofjustice.com/rules.php\" target=\"_blank\">http://chroniclesofjustice.com/rules.php</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh that seems pretty cool. I'm definitely bookmarking that for later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T10:36:18-07:00","id":976006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/975783-is-there-a-superhero-supervillan-game-similar-to-cofd?p=975842#post975842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really enjoy Supers as a genre, and I have played a good number of supers systems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you post on the Atomic Think Tank?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T11:14:55-07:00","id":976021,"title":"","content":"<b>RE: Atomic Think Tank</b><br /> <br /> I don't post on Atomic Think Tank, but I lurk there regularly when I need an idea of how to build a particular powerset. A fantastic resource!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T22:58:33-07:00","id":976373,"title":"","content":"CofD superhero game? Look no further than Mage!<br /> (On a more serious note though, Deviant seems very fitting, since you can probably make all the most popular superheroes as Deviants, or, if you don't want to wait for so long, there's a plentiful of options given above, from Aberrant to M&amp;M)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T02:51:44-07:00","id":976435,"title":"","content":"The mage chroniclers guide has a setting hack for playing mages as superheroes.<br /> <br /> If mages aren't your cup of tea for whatever reason, the superhero rules could be used for say hunters, dark heroes, or deviants (when that comes out).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T01:24:16-07:00","id":978919,"title":"","content":"Second Sight and Supernatural Merits are a thing yo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T15:27:13-07:00","id":986435,"title":"","content":"For a super-hero game by itself, only with the rules of CoD (instead of a super-hero game in the setting proper of the CoD), I will echo the vote for Mage. You don't have to explain the powers as magic, just use the rules. Mirrors does precisely that in its own &quot;official&quot; supers hack. Maybe you could take something out from Ascension to help.<br /> <br /> Aberrant or Scion can make for games a little more distinct in the rules, but already made for supers.<br /> <br /> If you don't see the need to keep with CoD rules, just know them better, I think Mutants and Masterminds is easy enough to learn and play, and almost perfect to do the job. I particularly suggest the 2nd Edition, not the 3rd.<br /> <br /> Will see this link of yours latter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}